### Delegate SD-JWT
* **Presenter:** Gareth Thomas
* **Slides:** [Delegate SD-JWT](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-oauth-sessa-delegate-sd-jwt-00)
* **Draft Reference:** `draft-ietf-oauth-delegate-sd-jwt`
* **Overview:** Defines an extension to SD-JWT (RFC 9901) to enable chaining/delegation by converting key-binding JWTs into nested SD-JWTs, supporting agent authorization, payment delegation, and digital credentials.
* **Key Updates & Scope Adjustments:**
  * Transitioning presentation protocol details (e.g., OpenID for VP) out of the core specification into agnostic requirements, leaving protocol-specific bindings to respective presentation specs.
  * Establishing core delegation policy constraints (e.g., expiration limits, delegation depth, delegate audience) within the spec, while leaving domain-specific business logic to application layers.
  * Documenting relationships and mapping rules with `draft-ietf-oauth-sd-jwt-vc`.
  * Refactoring the internal token structure to improve compatibility with standard SD-JWT libraries.
  * Distinguishing explicitly between keys used for delegation versus standard presentation key-binding.

