### Deferred Token Response
* **Presenter:** Devin (on behalf of authors)
* **Slides:** [Deferred Token Response](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-oauth-sessa-deferred-token-response-01)
* **Draft Reference:** `draft-ietf-oauth-deferred-token-response`
* **Updates:**
  * Integrated interactive response capabilities (formerly JAGAR) into the Deferred Token Response (DTR) draft to support out-of-band user confirmation during deferred flows.
* **Discussion on Open Issues:**
  * **Redirect URI in Interactive Mode:** Discussed parameter naming conflicts when combining interactive deferred modes with authorization code grants. Nick Watson recommended supporting redirect parameters across all grant types under a distinct parameter name.
  * **Callback / Notification Security:** Addressing security concerns raised by Brian Campbell regarding client-generated callback notification tokens. The proposed solution (suggested by Karl McGuinness) shifts notification token generation to the AS.
  * **Authorization Endpoint Deferral:**
    * *Option A:* Restrict core deferred token mechanisms strictly to the `/token` endpoint (no changes).
    * *Option B:* Allow deferral directly at the `/authorize` endpoint.
    * *Outcome:* Nick Watson, Jeff Lombardo, and Brian Campbell spoke in favor of Option A (restricting deferral to the `/token` endpoint).
  * **Scope Reduction:** Discussed splitting the callback notification mechanism into a separate document to keep the core DTR specification simple.

